---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pathTo } from '../lib/paths';
const experience = [
  ['Dec 2024 — present', 'Technical Services Lead', 'Data & Integrations · JustGo Technologies', 'Hands-on implementation, integration design, production delivery, international technical consultancy, code review, recruitment, and mentoring.'],
  ['Jan — Nov 2024', 'Senior Engineer', 'Data Services · JustGo Technologies', 'Greater responsibility for relational migrations, C#/.NET automation, bulk processing, data integrity, and connected platforms.'],
  ['Apr 2022 — Dec 2023', 'L2 Engineer', 'Data Services · JustGo Technologies', 'Built T-SQL transformations, database utilities, reporting and scheduled processing, and supported migration delivery.'],
  ['May — Aug 2021', 'Undergraduate Teaching Assistant', 'American International University–Bangladesh', 'Supported Data Structures and Computer Organization & Architecture teaching, laboratory work, and student problem-solving.']
];
---
<Layout title="About & experience">
  <header class="wrap page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">About / The person behind the work</p><h1>Engineering with context.</h1><p class="lead">I’m Md. Salimullah, a Bangladesh-based engineer and Technical Services Lead specialising in Data & Integrations at JustGo Technologies.</p></header>
  <section class="wrap about-intro"><div class="prose"><h2>What I care about</h2><p>Much of my work happens at the boundaries: between legacy data and a new platform, between an API and the organisation consuming it, or between a technical decision and the people affected by it.</p><p>I started with SQL transformations and operational data work. Over time, my responsibilities expanded into backend services, cloud automation, integration design, customer technical consultancy, and helping a team deliver reliably.</p><p>I value a clear account of what happened, a testable explanation of why, and a solution that someone else can maintain. That same perspective is shaping my move toward research in data science and healthcare AI.</p></div><aside class="about-facts"><p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p><dl><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Bangladesh</dd><dt>Professional focus</dt><dd>Data engineering, backend systems & interoperability</dd><dt>Research direction</dt><dd>Trustworthy AI for healthcare</dd><dt>Education</dt><dd>BSc, Computer Science & Engineering<br />AIUB · December 2021</dd></dl></aside></section>
  <section class="wrap section" id="experience"><p class="eyebrow">Experience</p><h2>A growing scope of responsibility.</h2><div class="timeline">{experience.map(([date, title, context, description]) => <article><p class="mono small">{date}</p><div><h3>{title}</h3><p class="timeline-context">{context}</p><p>{description}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">Working toolkit</p><h2>Tools follow the problem.</h2><div class="question-grid"><article><h3>Data & software</h3><p>SQL Server, T-SQL, relational modelling, C#/.NET, Python, ETL, REST APIs, data validation and reconciliation.</p></article><article><h3>Cloud & interoperability</h3><p>Azure Functions, WebJobs, Service Bus, Key Vault, background processing, webhooks, identity mapping and secure transfer.</p></article><article><h3>Research & practice</h3><p>PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, comparative evaluation, technical writing, code review, mentoring and delivery planning.</p></article></div><p class="small">This is a map of tools used across my work, rather than a self-rated proficiency score.</p></section>
  <div class="wrap contact-band"><h2>Have something<br />worth figuring out?</h2><a class="button" href={pathTo('contact/')}>Let’s talk ↗</a></div>
</Layout>
